9d73-a0a410023af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/assets/8bd5b7575d1693935df0d25a259767f0dd267fc1153139cd55cebad75e3988fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294521} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd703c1e-63b2-52c8-a661-5fd74717d952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0a69704c-1c6e-5b5d-ae42-82a5a6cd1452" :question/math-academy-id "q-122810" :question/problem "Which of the following could be the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-y?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by plotting some level curves of the function:\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=-1,$ we get ${x}^{2}-y=-1,$ which gives the parabola $y={x}^{2}+1$\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=0,$ we get ${x}^{2}-y=0,$ that is, the parabola $y={x}^{2}$\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=2,$ we get ${x}^{2}-y=2,$ that is, the parabola $y={x}^{2}-2$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nContinuing in this way, we get the following contour plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/assets/77a54ef31c41e0246e3d337a69c7faa161194058e6a5c672ef24d86866a83faf.png)\n\nNote that $f(x,y)$ increases as we move downward and away from the origin $O.$ \n\nNow, we recall the following facts:\n\n- The gradient field vectors of a function $f(x,y)$ always lie perpendicular to its level curves.\n\n- Moreover, the vectors point in the direction where $f(x,y)$ increases.\n\nWith this in mind, we can add the vector field to the contour plot, giving the following picture.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/assets/4e124d5e77ef9a28002aba9aac40f0b7eff1232dd1c08b6bca10b166469675c7.png)\n\nSo, the corresponding gradient field is as follows:\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/assets/8bd5b7575d1693935df0d25a259767f0dd267fc1153139cd55cebad75e3988fd.png)"}]}
